      "speech": "It has limits. DMT optimizes per video and beats us on text-to-video motion transfer, 0.85 versus 0.70. Motion finer than the latent grid is only approximated. Flow is 2D, so it can't say what's behind something or what appears. And every base model needs its own fine-tune. Still, it was a CVPR oral, and follow-ups like WonderPlay use it as their motion-to-video stage."
